  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Third Sunday of Lent” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Jesus was casting out a demon, and it was mute. And when He had cast out the demon, the mute man spoke, and the multitudes marveled. But some of them said: He casts out demons by Beelzebub, the prince of demons. And others, tempting Him, asked of Him a sign from heaven. But He, seeing their thoughts, said to them: Every kingdom divided against itself will be brought to desolation, and house upon house will fall. And if Satan also is divided against himself, how will his kingdom stand? For you say that through Beelzebub I cast out demons. Now if I cast out demons by Beelzebub, by whom do your children cast them out? Therefore they will be your judges. But if I cast out demons by the finger of God, doubtless the kingdom of God has come upon you. When a strong man armed keeps his court, those things are in peace which he possesses. But if one stronger than he comes upon him and overcomes him, he will take away all his armor in which he trusted, and will distribute his spoils. He who is not with Me is against Me; and he who does not gather with Me scatters. When the unclean spirit has gone out of a man, he walks through places without water, seeking rest; and not finding, he says: I will return into my house from which I came out. And when he comes, he finds it swept and adorned. Then he goes and takes with him seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and entering in they dwell there; and the last state of that man becomes worse than the first. And it came to pass, as He spoke these things, that a certain woman from the crowd, lifting up her voice, said to Him: Blessed is the womb that bore You, and the breasts that nursed You. But He said: Yes, rather, blessed are those who hear the word of God and keep it.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w004", "w005", "w006"], "anchor": "w006", "gloss": "Jesus was casting out" }, { "words": ["w016", "w017"], "anchor": "w016", "gloss": "spoke" }, { "words": ["w020", "w021"], "anchor": "w020", "gloss": "wondered" }, { "words": ["w023", "w024"], "anchor": "w023", "gloss": "But some" }, { "words": ["w047", "w048"], "anchor": "w047", "gloss": "their thoughts" }, { "words": ["w062", "w063"], "anchor": "w062", "gloss": "And if" }, { "words": ["w068", "w069"], "anchor": "w068", "gloss": "is divided" }, { "words": ["w072", "w073"], "anchor": "w072", "gloss": "his kingdom" }, { "words": ["w088", "w089"], "anchor": "w088", "gloss": "your children" }, { "words": ["w095", "w096"], "anchor": "w095", "gloss": "your judges" }, { "words": ["w115", "w116"], "anchor": "w115", "gloss": "his court" }, { "words": ["w123", "w124"], "anchor": "w123", "gloss": "But if" }, { "words": ["w131", "w132"], "anchor": "w131", "gloss": "his armor" }, { "words": ["w138", "w139"], "anchor": "w138", "gloss": "his spoils" }, { "words": ["w142", "w143"], "anchor": "w143", "gloss": "is not" }, { "words": ["w150", "w151"], "anchor": "w151", "gloss": "does not gather" }, { "words": ["w172", "w173"], "anchor": "w172", "gloss": "my house" }, { "words": ["w202", "w203"], "anchor": "w202", "gloss": "of that man" }, { "words": ["w206", "w207"], "anchor": "w206", "gloss": "It came to pass" }, { "words": ["w222", "w223", "w224"], "anchor": "w224", "gloss": "that bore You" }] }
